    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change assigns each new owner a `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` at creation time, and exposes it on the owner read model.\n\n**Domain model** (`Owner.java`)\n- Added a persisted `customerCode` field mapped to a new `customer_code` column, with getter/setter, and included it in `toString()`.\n\n**Schema** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four DB schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) so every profile stays consistent (tests run on hsqldb).\n\n**API contract** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema, alongside the existing derived `displayName`/`initials`. The generated `OwnerDto` picks it up and MapStruct maps it by name automatically, so it's returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Counting owners** \u2014 added a `count()` method to the `OwnerRepository` interface with implementations in all three persistence layers (JPA, JDBC, and an explicit `@Query` on the Spring Data repo), surfaced through the service facade as `ClinicService.countOwners()`.\n\n**Code generation** \u2014 a new single-responsibility `CustomerCodeGenerator` component builds the code: upper-cased first three letters of the last name, a hyphen, and `count + 1` zero-padded to 4 digits (`String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`).\n\n**Wiring** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2014 after the existing validation/normalization/registration-date defaulting, it assigns `owner.setCustomerCode(generator.generate(lastName, clinicService.countOwners()))` before saving. Because the count is taken before each save, the second owner created sees a count one higher, giving the global sequence the spec requires.\n\nThe acceptance test (`SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and consecutive global sequence) and the full suite pass.",
